        "explanation": {
          "text": "Fractions are a way to show part of a whole. Imagine you have a pizza that is cut into 8 slices, and you eat 2 of them. You can write this as a fraction: 2/8. The top number, 2, tells us how many slices you ate, and the bottom number, 8, tells us how many slices there were in total. We can also simplify fractions to make them easier to understand. For example, 2/8 can be simplified to 1/4 because both numbers can be divided by 2.",
